WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.130
Go to the Lungfish Genome Explorer website and click the current Stable release.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.724
If Safari asks, allow the download.

00:00:11.724 --> 00:00:16.172
It needs a Mac with Apple Silicon running macOS 26 or later.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.389
Double-click the downloaded disk image, the file ending in .dmg.

00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:25.959
In the window that appears, drag Lungfish onto the Applications folder.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.983
Open the app named Lungfish from your Applications folder.

00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:36.260
If macOS asks whether to open an app downloaded from the internet, click Open.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.162
The Welcome window opens.

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:41.973
Under Third-Party Tools, click Install.

00:00:41.973 --> 00:00:48.243
LGE downloads the analysis programs it runs, such as read aligners and variant callers.

00:00:48.243 --> 00:00:51.991
This takes several minutes, and you do it only once.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.479
Click Create Project, type a name, and click Save.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.710
A project is one folder on your Mac.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.937
It holds your data and your results as you work.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:15.209
Next, watch Your first project on the Videos page of the Lungfish Genome Explorer website.
